WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:01.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome back.
-Thank you.

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So this is now --
-I love it in scenes

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
where they write
the name of the person

00:00:04.237 --> 00:00:05.238 line:92%
you're supposed to be discussing

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
on a big piece of paper
as Hangman.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.042 line:92%
"David can't remember his lines.

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's do a whole episode
of Hangman.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.213
-Oh, so you're the kind of actor
that just loves it --

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:15.682
If it's right there on paper,
you don't have to rehearse.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.919
-Well, many times, I want to be
the actor who cheats that way,

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:20.587 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
like on a computer.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:24.357
And I'll write what I'm supposed
to be seeing on the computer

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
or commenting on the computer,
on the computer,

00:00:27.127 --> 00:00:30.096
and then I'll start to feel so
guilty that I'm a crappy actor

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I should've
memorized my line.

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:33.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then my eyes
have gotten worse,

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.635 size:75% position:38%
so I can't even read
what I've written.

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:36.169 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:39.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
My handwriting is so bad
and so small, and I'm there,

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.107 line:92%
and I don't know my lines now,

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
and everybody knows
that I'm a crappy actor,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I've been trying to cheat,
and it's just awful.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:49.049 size:81% position:41%
-Well, I don't think
you're a crappy actor.

00:00:49.049 --> 00:00:49.582 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well, thanks.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:52.118
-I do think you should have
figured all this out by now.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.254
Because this is now 25 years...
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.254 --> 00:00:56.689 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, true.
-...25 years of Mulder.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:58.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did you ever think --
I mean, no one thinks this,

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:01.528
but what's it been like to play
a character for this long,

00:01:01.528 --> 00:01:02.195 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and has it been nice

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have the breaks
that you've had, obviously?

00:01:04.631 --> 00:01:06.766 size:78% position:39%
Because it's not been
25 years straight.

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:09.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like Mulder, again.
Yeah.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:10.970 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Yeah, it's -- it's --

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:12.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know
that I can compare it

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
to anybody else's job,
because, you know,

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
I started playing
this guy in '93.

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:20.380
And he has a certain kind of,
like, anti-establishment energy.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would've
had to have had that, too.

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.517 line:92%
You know, I auditioned for it

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:26.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
irreverently in a tie
with pigs on it.

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You wore a pig tie
when you auditioned?

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I thought that was,
like, irreverent.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:31.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Did they like that?

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.693
Did they say, "You're our guy,"
when they saw it?

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. They said,
"We thought you were our guy

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
until we saw the pig tie."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:40.600
And then, you know, now
I'm playing him 25 years later,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.837
and he's still -- he's still
kind of anti-establishment.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:47.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you can't play it
with the same kind of energy

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.007 line:92%
that you do as a young man.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:52.579
It has to have ripened into
some other kind of decrepitude.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:53.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it's like
an energetic decrepitude,

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:56.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you know what I'm saying.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.318 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So that's really
what I've been trying to find

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:00.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
is an energetic decrepitude.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:01.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's seems like something
worth fighting for.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel like, in this moment
right here, I found it.

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:06.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:08.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-An interesting thing
that's happened is it feels

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:14.300
like the world has caught up to
the Mulder world view in 1993

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.135 line:92%
of "Don't trust the government."

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:19.506
That now seems to be, like,
a platform you can even run on.

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, it is interesting,
because when we first started

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:24.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing the reboot,
I was like, "Oh, my God.

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:28.181
Is Mulder kind of in league
with President [bleep] hole?"

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:31.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And by the way,
I think the word

00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:34.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're looking for
is [bleep] blank.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Oh! You think we should

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:36.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
just go [bleep] blank?
Yeah.

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[Bleep] blank
is perfectly acceptable.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right. Now that's
like a game of Hangman.

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[Bleep] blank.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:44.664 size:88% position:44% line:92%
[Bleep] blank countries.

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:48.234
Since "hole" or "house" is the
one that's open to conjecture.

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:49.435 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, exactly.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I think, you know,
Mulder was saying

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the government
is lying about aliens

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:55.708 size:75% position:38% line:92%
and stuff like that.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.743 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And what is coming out

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
of President [bleep] hole's
White House

00:02:59.245 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they're delegitimizing
every news source.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's not just aliens.
Yeah.

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Actually, aliens is the only
thing they're giving us.

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.292 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-You know, so...

00:03:12.292 --> 00:03:14.527
-You obviously spent a lot
of time with this character.

00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:18.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think Mulder
is a good FBI agent?

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's the worst.
-Yeah.

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:24.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We've done about 200 --
I think 213 or 218 episodes.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:28.274
-Yeah.
-And he has solved nary a case.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.576 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.576 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's really
the opposite of "Law &amp; Order."

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.347 line:92%
It never ends in a courtroom.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's like
no laws and no order.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.951 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
No arrests.
25 years, and no arrests.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Damn it! Again."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:45.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and it's like, by
the fourth season of the show,

00:03:45.592 --> 00:03:46.759 line:92%
like, we've become a big hit,

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:49.729
and it started to reflect
in the writing a little bit

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
where Gillian Anderson's
character and I

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
would walk into a scene,
and people would go,

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, my God.
It's Mulder and Scully,"

00:03:55.802 --> 00:03:57.136 line:92%
and I'm like, "No, no, no!"

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "Ugh.
It's Mulder and Scully."

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-But it was like

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:03.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
the real-world appreciation
of our characters

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:06.779 align:start size:94% position:6%
that kind of infected --
-The fake FBI.

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:07.447 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Now it's a really --

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
This should be
Trump's favorite show.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:10.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
One, you don't trust
the government.

00:04:10.683 --> 00:04:11.751 line:92%
And, two, you're an FBI agent

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
who doesn't know
what he's doing.

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:16.322
Trump's like, "This is what I've
been saying about everything!"

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:21.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you --
-Well, we didn't --

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:22.829 line:92%
We didn't shoot a scene --

00:04:22.829 --> 00:04:24.197 line:92%
Like, our boss is named Skinner,

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he always has
the President's picture.

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:29.602 size:78% position:39%
So we've had Clinton,
and we've had Bush,

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:31.104 line:92%
and we've had Obama, even.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we've had three --
And I was --

00:04:32.438 --> 00:04:36.342
I was so terrified that we were
gonna have to shoot a scene --

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:39.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you shot around it?
-With Orange Julius.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:40.313 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh...
I don't know.

00:04:42.715 --> 00:04:43.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess we weren't
in Skinner's office,

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:46.653
so we kind of got away with it.
-Oh, good.

